Compat before-patch for b6d536-chat-controller-step56-seam, applied to d3fe74ef2 (the parent of the
lane commit 0b7b9df44 that introduced the repaired behaviour; coordinator decision 2).

Production, one constructor only: RuntimeReconciler's lease-free Engine constructor, which later
checks call (5e4f4e698 deleted the lease). It delegates to this state's own Engine constructor with
a fresh RuntimeGpuLease, as ServicePhase builds it, so the reconciler drives its control exactly as
this state does. No production code in this state calls it, and it supplies no stop-before-launch or
embedding hand-off behaviour.

Test helper, before-API variant (passed through this patch, not as an overlay): ManagedChatSeam as
the candidate has it, without its ChildControl branch (this state's factory takes
ManagedChildRegistry; the named checks never pass a ChildControl). It changes no assertion.

